 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Bring them in and have them chilled in the fridge for an hour or two. Then warm up the pan with a few spoons of oil. You can use a little bit of oil to help them slide in, but too much will make them greasy. Pop a couple of sticks on each side and they' stay up pretty well. You can also use a little bit of tape for the back as a last resort. Then save them for a calmer night. A big pan of garlic and onion with them is worth it on a cold night.",
